#' Field description: observed dropout proportion 2
#' @field observedDropoutProportion2 Mean replication-specific cumulative observed dropout proportion in arm 2 at each stage, counting dropout before the event and by that stage's analysis time. Only replications contributing at that stage with a finite analysis time and positive enrolled-subject denominator contribute; NA if none contribute. Stopped trials and discontinued groups do not contribute to later stages; overlapping populations include their shared subjects. Numeric matrices with stage rows and scenario columns for two-arm trials. In multi-arm trials, arm 1 has dimensions stage, scenario, and active arm; arm 2 is a stage-by-scenario matrix for shared control. In enrichment trials, both arms have dimensions stage, scenario, and population (subpopulations followed by the full population). A single active arm or population uses a stage-by-scenario matrix. Stage and scenario dimensions are always retained. NULL for test-statistic-based simulation. Both proportions are hidden in print and summary output when both input dropout rates are zero, but remain in the object.
#' @keywords internal
